codex_reading:
\hand{* That $E^{(p)}$ represents $\psi^pE$ follows since $E \mapsto E^{(p)}$ defines a
homomorphism $K_{alg} \rightarrow K_{alg}$ which coincides with $\psi^p$ on line bundles,
together with the splitting principle: $K_{alg}(PE) \unsure{\cong|=} K_{alg}(X)[T]/(\lambda_{-T}(E))$.}

final_reading:
\handwritten{* That $E^{(p)}$ represents $\psi^pE$ follows since $E \mapsto E^{(p)}$ defines a
homomorphism $K_{alg} \rightarrow K_{alg}$ which coincides with $\psi^p$ on line bundles\unsure{;|,}
together with the splitting principle: $K_{alg}(PE) \cong K_{alg}(X)[T]/(\lambda_{-T}(E))$.}

